{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>Peoples will bow to you — and bow.</b> וישתחו is written וישתחוו is read. <b>Be a master to your brothers.</b> His judgment concurred with the decree that the older shall serve the younger." "<b>Be a master.</b> 'Be a master' — it is in the language of granting." "<b>Sons of your mother.</b> If she remarries after my death." "<b>Those who curse you — cursed.</b> According to the plain sense, Isaac thought he was Esau, and he knew that he was hated, and even so, though he was pious in his eyes, he is nevertheless a man of the outdoors and was accustomed to forests. Therefore he put his curse before his blessing and said it in plural language. But Abraham — it was known that he was beloved, and not many would curse him, so his verse is written in singular language: 'and whoever curses you — I will curse.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:18.316095782Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}